though (worst meaning closer to cursed).

As to WHAT, precisely, a luckstone does, well, that's a spoiler:


(spoiler!)





















Luck is a number, from -10 to +10, let's say, with negative being 'bad'
and positive being 'good.'  Every hundred turns or so, luck moves one
step towards zero...  Having a luckstone just affects how your luck times
out.  A cursed stone lets good luck time out, but not bad luck.  An
uncursed stone freezes your luck, wherever it may be.

A blessed stone, then, lets only bad luck time out.  Oh, and blessed stones
add some luck, cursed stones subtract some.

